<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line ltx_leqno" lang="en">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Combinatorics
and Hodge theory of degenerations of abelian varieties:
A survey of the Mumford construction</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Philip Engel
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>Department of Mathematics, Statistics,
and Computer Science, University of Illinois in Chicago (UIC),
851 S Morgan St, Chicago, IL 60607, USA
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:pengel@uic.edu">pengel@uic.edu</a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">, </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Olivier de Gaay Fortman
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>Department of Mathematics, Utrecht University, Budapestlaan 6, 3584 CD Utrecht, The Netherlands.
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:a.o.d.degaayfortman@uu.nl">a.o.d.degaayfortman@uu.nl</a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before"> and </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Stefan Schreieder
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_address"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Address: </span>Leibniz University Hannover, Institute of Algebraic Geometry, Welfengarten 1, 30167 Hannover, Germany.
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email address: </span><a href="mailto:schreieder@math.uni-hannover.de">schreieder@math.uni-hannover.de</a>
</span></span></span></span></div>
<div class="ltx_dates">Date: August 24, 2026</div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract.</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We survey the Mumford construction of degenerating
abelian varieties, with a focus on the analytic version
of the construction, and its relation to toric geometry. Moreover, we study the geometry and Hodge
theory of multivariable
degenerations of abelian varieties
associated to regular matroids, and
extend some fundamental results of Clemens
on <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-parameter semistable degenerations to the
multivariable setting.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Key words and phrases: </h6>Abelian varieties,
toric varieties, Hodge theory,
degenerations, matroids
</div>
<div class="ltx_classification"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_classification">2020 Mathematics Subject Classification</h6>14K10, 14K25,
14C30, 05B35, 32G20, 14M25
</div>
